# The Linux packaging revision: "<app version> <revision>".
#
# Bump the revision when the .deb, the tarball or the APT repository has to be rebuilt
# while the app itself is unchanged (a dependency, an installed file, the metainfo),
# so the new package has a version of its own and never replaces the published files
# of the same name. It applies only while the app version matches: once the csproj
# moves to a new version, packages are that version again with no suffix, whatever
# this file says. tools/linux/package-version.sh reads it.
#
# 2.0.0-2 (2026-09-19): Ubuntu 26.04's libicu78, a declared libssl, Installed-Size,
# and AppStream metainfo for software centres (#315-#318).
